  flavorList:
  - The syringe has a warning label but its scratched out...
  - A very practical design made popular by their inherent professionalism.
  - There is a small water bag inside that in constently heated by the radiation.
  - '"Not for human consumtion."'
  - '"Harder, better, faster, stronger."'
  - Aircraft grade metal also happens to be everything else grade metal.
  - Good thing it's one size fits all.
  - Also happens to be a great cooking oil.
  - Now the gun knows where it's aiming.
  - It's like shooting mini planes.
  - Metal-dynamics have become a huge reaserching topic for many of war machines
    recently.
  - Bullets so heavy gravity actualy agknowledges them now
  - looks like a bathroom tile.
  - Follow your heart.
  - Seems an octopus has taken this expired radioactive fuel cell as a home, don't
    worry radiation is good for sea life.
  - Hes a friendly little guy.
  - Hey more firepower is more firepower.
  - I heard the organic ones get better with time, just watch out for the meat flavor...
  - '"Aw man."'
  - A heavy weight lifted.
  - Comfy cozy and pre-warmed!
  - we had to find some use for the nuclear waste.
  - Just what you don't need.
  - If you're cold their cold, give them direct acsess to your bloodstream.
  - '"I am NOT doing that..." "AND JUST LET THEM STARVE!?"'
  - This appears to be a textbook printed onto standard paper and stapled together,
    reasonable looking the the current prices...
  - 
  - 
  - "the bullets are dipped in a advanced jamming substance manufactured organicly
    from \"Fragaria \xD7 ananassa\", an excotic biological substance commanly added
    to food products."
  - Ammo storage is what it's all a-belt.
  - Don't hold near any vital organs or limbs for a period of more than 10 seconds.
  - Light as a bird.
  - Light as a bat.
  - A vital component for large scale factories, also happens to be usefull for autoloading
    firearms!
  - FIREPOWER(tm) used to be a heating and cooling instalation buissness before the
    war. When they saw the profits of what their exceptional heating elements could
    bring when used in war, it was a easy desicion to shift into munitions!
  - 
